title: "Actions Workflow Map: Repository-Wide GitHub Actions Visualization and Analysis"
type: software
version: "0.2.1"
date-released: "2026-07-28"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21641546"

authors:
  - family-names: "Srivastava"
    given-names: "Tanya"
    affiliation: "Independent Developer"

abstract: >-
  Actions Workflow Map is an independently developed, open-source,
  local-first developer tool that converts GitHub Actions workflow
  configurations into visual and machine-readable operational maps.
  It supports individual workflow analysis and repository-wide discovery,
  including workflow triggers, jobs, needs dependencies, strategy matrices,
  local reusable workflows, permissions, concurrency groups, environments,
  external action references, and artifact producer-consumer relationships.
  The software generates Mermaid diagrams, self-contained HTML reports,
  JSON reports, console summaries, and deterministic evidence-linked
  findings to improve workflow comprehension, reviewability, observability,
  traceability, validation reliability, and developer productivity.

